Implement user story SKY-004-be-impl: Implement Express server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard — BE Impl

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts with all route handlers, middleware, env config, and build setup. Export `app` for testing; guard `listen()`; gate API routes on RAPIDAPI_KEY; serve dashboard from file; ensure build copies static assets.

## Acceptance Criteria
- 1. src/server.ts exports named `app` (Express instance) separately from `listen()`; `listen()` guarded by main-module check so vitest never binds a port
- 2. GET /health → 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }, never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- 3. GET / → 200 text/html from src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync (or equivalent); no hardcoded/duplicated inline HTML string; never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- 4. GET /search valid params (from, to, date, adults) → 200 JSON { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO-8601 }; count === flights.length; missing/empty required param (from, to, date) → 400 JSON { error }; invalid date → 400 JSON { error }; adults defaults to 1, non-positive-integer values → 400 JSON { error }
- 5. GET /cheapest valid params → 200 JSON with single cheapest FlightResult; no flights → 404 JSON { error }; missing/empty required param → 400 JSON { error }; invalid date → 400 JSON { error }; adults defaults to 1
- 6. RAPIDAPI_KEY absent at startup → /search and /cheapest return 503 JSON { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / unaffected; RAPIDAPI_KEY value never appears in any response body or error message
- 7. SkyscannerClient throws during /search or /cheapest → 500 JSON { error: string } without crashing or unhandled rejection; FlightResult imported from SKY-002 type export, not redeclared inline
- 8. PORT read from env (default 3000); package.json has 'start' script (node dist/server.js) and 'build' script; build copies src/public/ into dist/public/ so dist/public/index.html exists and GET / serves the real file after build





